From d79820f5f31a8d63d1f5b19374733a240f96b02d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:37:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 57/87] drivers: sunxi-cir: a fresh decoder and an empty FIFO
 at each probe

The decoder state lives in the device's static state and the probe
cleared neither it nor the receiver FIFO. On the H713 the probe runs at
every suspend (cir_get() in h713_suspend_prepare): a frame cut off by
the last wake, or samples Linux left in the FIFO, made the first IR
press of the next standby decode against stale state, and it was lost
(PRUEFUNG5 CS-16).

The probe now zeroes the decoder context field by field (a compound
literal would need memset) and reads the FIFO empty, at most 64
samples, before it enables the module.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/cir/sunxi-cir.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/cir/sunxi-cir.c b/drivers/cir/sunxi-cir.c
index a104a2c..bc98d9a 100644
--- a/drivers/cir/sunxi-cir.c
+++ b/drivers/cir/sunxi-cir.c
@@ -81,6 +81,20 @@ sunxi_cir_probe(const struct device *dev)
 	mmio_write_32(self->regs + CIR_RXCFG,
 	              CONFIG(CIR_USE_OSC24M) ? 0x00001404 : 0x010f0310);
 
+	/*
+	 * Start each suspend with a fresh decoder and an empty FIFO: what is
+	 * left from the last one, or from Linux using the receiver, is not
+	 * the start of a frame. The FIFO holds 64 samples at most.
+	 */
+	state->dec_ctx.buffer  = 0;
+	state->dec_ctx.counter = 0;
+	state->dec_ctx.bits    = 0;
+	state->dec_ctx.state   = 0;
+	state->dec_ctx.pulse   = 0;
+	state->dec_ctx.width   = 0;
+	for (int n = 0; n < 64 && mmio_read_32(self->regs + CIR_RXSTA) >> 8; ++n)
+		mmio_read_32(self->regs + CIR_RXFIFO);
+
 	/* Enable CIR module. */
 	mmio_write_32(self->regs + CIR_RXCTL, 0x33);
 
